    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Provide primary caregivers of children younger than 23 months with behavior-changing communication regarding optimal Martenal Infant Young Child (MIYC) feeding practices.  - Provide sanitation, hygiene promotion, GBV prevention- Refer caretakers of children with acute malnourished children to MPC activities                                            - Screen and enroll children with SAM into the   Outpatient Therapeutic feeding program (OTP)                      - Screen and enroll children with MAM into the Targeted Supplementary Feeding Program (TSFP).- Refer SAM children with complications to stabilization units.- Refer malnourished PLWs for supplementary feeding. - Support the Community Health Workers (CHWs) to conduct community screening, detection, and referrals of children and PLW with malnutrition.&quot;</narrative>
